Conversation content on Day 55: [|User|]: Dislikes Review:

1. Final Dawn: Season 1 (The Thrilling Post-Apocalyptic Series): {'overall': 1.0, 'Review_text': 'This IS NOT A THRILLING POST-APOCALYPTIC SERIES. This novel skipped around way too much and does not come close to preppers trying to survive. This is more science fiction, and not even good science fiction. I knew I should of stopped reading after reading about the " silvery floating globes" . Trust me, there are way better books than this. Don't waste your time and money.'}

2. The Beginning Of The End: {'overall': 1.0, 'Review_text': 'Sorry, this book just couldn't keep my attention. It skipped around way too much between the characters. Maybe if the story focused on one character it might have been more readable. I just plain got bored after 100 pages and could not go back and read it.'}

Other Review:

1. Last Stand: Patriots: {'overall': 5.0, 'Review_text': "If you like the first book, you'll like the next three. The action and plot just accelerates from now on. The author continues to maintain the reader's interest with prepping tips and living off the land and while maintaining an entertaining style of writing that is not preachy or too deep into esoteric topics which tend to bog down a story. He does a great job of capturing the spirit of patriots and what makes this a great country at its heart."}

2. Final Dawn: Season 1 (The Thrilling Post-Apocalyptic Series): {'overall': 4.0, 'Review_text': "This book ended up being nothing at all like what I thought it would be. I expected a normal post-apocalyptic story, with the usual bad guys dropping the bombs... not the case. While there were times things got just a little too technical for me, or just a bit too unbelievable, I still enjoyed the story. I can't imagine anyone being able to stop reading this without finding out what the swarms were. That alone was enough to make me finish the season, but I also really liked the characters. The dialogue could get kind of cheesy and overly dramatic, but I chose to ignore that. Overall, I definitely recommend this! I purchased it on a whim (mainly because the cover caught my eye), and am glad I gave it a shot. I'm really looking forward Episode 6."}

3. The Beginning Of The End: {'overall': 5.0, 'Review_text': "I am a LONG time reader of 'End Times' type novels and this one was exceptionally good. It has twists and turns that surprised me and that seldom happens anymore. On a technical note there are some editing issues but not enough to take away the enjoyment of reading the book and I only mention this because some writers want to know there are mistakes so they can fix them. Now, my only question is - is there going to be a sequel or is there one out now? I'm doing the review from my Kindle Fire HD so I can't just pop out and see : ) I highly recommend this book to anyone who likes End Times books but also for those who are looking to get an idea of what's going on behind the scenes, if you will, of our world today. I think he's pegged it pretty good."}

